1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,460
Your cut of twenty trillion dollars is smaller than you think.

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:08,160
Forbes counts three thousand four hundred twenty-eight billionaires.

3
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:10,420
All together, they're worth twenty point one trillion dollars.

4
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:14,640
A trillion is a thousand billions, which is ridiculous.

5
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:18,180
But real talk, it's mostly company shares, not cash.

6
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:21,720
Now pretend it's cash, split evenly, handed out once.

7
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:24,400
Double-tap if you already know what you'd buy first.

8
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:28,600
Divide by every human alive, about eight point two billion people.

9
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:32,640
Newborns, grandmas, you, your weird uncle, same check.

10
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:35,520
And the check says about two thousand four hundred fifty dollars.

11
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:39,260
That's not monthly, it's one time. Damn.

12
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:42,520
Now send this to the friend who swears we'd all be millionaires.

13
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:45,960
Stretch it across a year, it's six seventy-two a day.

14
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:48,500
Basically a sandwich a day, then it's gone.

15
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:52,980
Plot twist: that list grew about four trillion dollars in one year.

16
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:56,240
That growth alone is four hundred eighty-eight dollars a person.

17
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:59,060
Follow, 'cause the last one's the craziest.

18
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:02,240
The average billionaire? Almost five point nine billion dollars.

19
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:06,260
That's two point four million people's checks, stacked up.

20
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:10,200
Big pile, sure. But eight billion is a hell of a lot of slices.

21
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,620
So would your cut change your year?

